{"ISBN:9780691005423":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9780691005423","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL7755997M/Rethinking_Gnosticism","preview":"restricted","preview_url":"https://archive.org/details/rethinkinggnosti0000will","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/439574-S.jpg","details":{"publishers":["Princeton University Press"],"number_of_pages":356,"table_of_contents":[{"level":0,"label":"","title":"What Kind of Thing Do Scholars Mean by \"Gnosticism\"?: A Look at Four Cases","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"\"Gnosticism\" as a Category","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Protest Exegesis? or Hermeneutical Problem-Solving?","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Parasites? or Innovators?","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Anticosmic World-Rejection? or Sociocultural Accommodation?","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Hatred of the Body? or the Perfection of the Human?","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Asceticism...?","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"...or Libertinism?","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Deterministic Elitism? or Inclusive Theories of Conversion?","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Where They Came From...","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"...and What They Left Behind","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}}],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Most anyone interested in such topics as creation mythology, Jungian theory, or the idea of \"secret teachings\" in ancient Judaism and Christianity has found \"gnosticism\" compelling. Yet the term \"gnosticism,\" which often connotes a single rebellious movement against the prevailing religions of late antiquity, gives the false impression of a monolithic religious phenomenon. Here Michael Williams challenges the validity of the widely invoked category of ancient \"gnosticism\" and the ways it has been described. Presenting such famous writings and movements as the Apocryphon of John and Valentinian Christianity, Williams uncovers the similarities and differences among some major traditions widely categorized as gnostic. He provides an eloquent, systematic argument for a more accurate way to discuss these interpretive approaches.\r\n\r\nThe modern construct \"gnosticism\" is not justified by any ancient self-definition, and many of the most commonly cited religious features that supposedly define gnosticism phenomenologically turn out to be questionable. Exploring the sample sets of \"gnostic\" teachings, Williams refutes generalizations concerning asceticism and libertinism, attitudes toward the body and the created world, and alleged features of protest, parasitism, and elitism. He sketches a fresh model for understanding ancient innovations on more \"mainstream\" Judaism and Christianity, a model that is informed by modern research on dynamics in new religious movements and is freed from the false stereotypes from which the category \"gnosticism\" has been constructed."},"weight":"14.4 ounces","isbn_10":["0691005427"],"covers":[439574],"physical_format":"Paperback","lc_classifications":["BT1390 .W475 1996"],"key":"/books/OL7755997M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL2769353A","name":"Michael Allen Williams"}],"subtitle":"An Argument for Dismantling a Dubious Category","subjects":["Gnosticism","Religious","Religion - World Religions","Religion","History","History & Surveys - Ancient & Classical","Archaeology and Ancient History","Jewish Studies","Mind, Body, Spirit","Philosophy","Religion / History","Reference"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"first_sentence":{"type":"/type/text","value":"One of the most interesting developments in the history of religion in late antiquity was the emergence of certain forms of religious expression and practice that modern scholarship usually classifies under the rubric \"Gnosticism,\" or Gnosis,\" or \"the Gnostic religion.\""},"source_records":["marc:marc_claremont_school_theology/CSTMARC1_barcode.mrc:222932722:5094","bwb:9780691005423","marc:marc_claremont_school_theology/CSTMARC1_multibarcode.mrc:223206937:5094","ia:rethinkinggnosti0000will","amazon:0691005427"],"title":"Rethinking \"Gnosticism\"","dewey_decimal_class":["299/.932 20"],"identifiers":{"goodreads":["650275"],"librarything":["69315"]},"isbn_13":["9780691005423"],"edition_name":"New Ed edition","lccn":["96006490"],"local_id":["urn:cst:10011444532"],"publish_date":"April 12, 1999","works":[{"key":"/works/OL8327389W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"physical_dimensions":"9 x 6 x 1 inches","ocaid":"rethinkinggnosti0000will","latest_revision":12,"revision":12,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-29T15:03:11.581851"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2022-10-30T10:34:27.598828"}}},"ISBN:9783788703677":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9783788703677","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL18605323M/Gnosis_und_Auferstehung","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL18605323M/Gnosis_und_Auferstehung","details":{"publishers":["Neukirchener Verlag"],"number_of_pages":212,"subtitle":"der Brief an Rheginus von Nag Hammadi; mit einem Anhange: Der koptische Text des Briefes an Rheginus","isbn_10":["3788703679"],"pagination":"212 p. ;","local_id":["urn:cst:10011366882"],"key":"/books/OL18605323M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL1993103A","name":"Malcolm Lee Peel"}],"publish_places":["Neukirchen"],"contributions":["Funk, Wolf-Peter."],"genres":["Early works to 1800."],"source_records":["marc:marc_claremont_school_theology/CSTMARC2_barcode.mrc:67523268:2134","marc:marc_claremont_school_theology/CSTMARC2_multibarcode.mrc:67555551:2134","marc:harvard_bibliographi